{"title":"2011 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, called the common difference. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/8/da82253c979ff59a2054e49bc8a8fd70e69d62e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5, 8, 11, 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> are the first five terms of an arithmetic sequence with a common difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e7679b01e114773e2822a8fd5615ea83def33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the 6<sup>th</sup> and 7<sup>th</sup> terms of the sequence given above.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f8473eac20565df46e727e7b9f14fca92a9ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the sequence. Since the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the starting term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a46921695c68bf025e53d3c4732ded01fb10ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k} = 3(k - 1) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958b780e9ac70afafb38024b316e3e0288979f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=3k - 3 + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c27bd721969775377c019995e3669717fa8fdd06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=3k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/5030b8b2e1983047683733deb951a552b42ed896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> for the sixth term, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57194d72bca8eb2dcf7e6d119891e4a000987ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{6} = 3 \\times 6 - 1 = \\boxed{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/869588262d13ad049e1639efd917b7eca81d1491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> for the seventh term, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be7e00a87b4ee44c19000e832e2603b3cdac262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{7} = 3 \\times 7 - 1 = \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the fifth term of the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sixth term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b11deb8178f9c81df93a12d8ee9b42d7fb5ade5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 + 3 = \\boxed{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Since the sixth term of the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the seventh term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3d61cd03da38cee648e533c95dd85f7ada1b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 3 = \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224758\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 95/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 435/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3541/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.725      1 2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.725      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36981:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224758 and revision id 285884. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}